{"parentUuid": "64f84672-6702-42c6-b630-0f18918c5349", "isSidechain": true, "agentId": "a7b723182a2d800b6", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "id": "msg_011CfjWy4nvYVgF5E6b4A3p8", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Qws7vGiwq37P3e5Vt8iMz2", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "/Users/me/demo4/docs/guide.md", "content": "# demo4 Usage Guide\n\n## Overview\ndemo4 is a lightweight Python project providing utility functions for basic mathematical operations and a simple entry point.\n\n## Project Structure\n- `src/main.py` - Main application entry point\n- `src/utils.py` - Utility functions for arithmetic operations\n- `data.txt` - Sample data file\n\n## Getting Started\n\n### Running the Main Application\nTo run the main application:\n```bash\npython src/main.py\n```\nThis will print \"hi\" to the console.\n\n## Using the Utility Functions\n\n### Importing Utils\nImport the utility module in your Python scripts:\n```python\nfrom src.utils import add, sub, mul, div\n```\n\n### Available Functions\n\n#### add(a, b)\nAdds two numbers and returns the result.\n```python\nresult = add(5, 3)  # Returns 8\n```\n\n#### sub(a, b)\nSubtracts b from a and returns the result.\n```python\nresult = sub(10, 4)  # Returns 6\n```\n\n#### mul(a, b)\nMultiplies two numbers and returns the product.\n```python\nresult = mul(6, 7)  # Returns 42\n```\n\n#### div(a, b)\nDivides a by b and returns the result. Raises ZeroDivisionError if b is zero.\n```python\nresult = div(20, 4)  # Returns 5.0\nresult = div(10, 0)  # Raises ZeroDivisionError\n```\n\n## Working with Data\nThe `data.txt` file contains sample data with Greek letters (alpha, beta, gamma, delta, epsilon). Use this file for testing data processing workflows.\n\n## Error Handling\nWhen using the `div()` function, always handle potential ZeroDivisionError:\n```python\ntry:\n    result = div(10, 0)\nexcept ZeroDivisionError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n```\n"}